# Clean Code: Functions

## Keep functions small

```php
// BAD - one massive method doing everything
public function processOrder(Order $order): void
{
    // 50+ lines handling validation, payment, notification, logging...
}

// GOOD - split into focused steps
public function processOrder(Order $order): void
{
    $this->validateOrder($order);
    $this->chargePayment($order);
    $this->sendConfirmation($order);
}
```

## Do one thing

```php
// BAD
public function saveUserAndSendEmail(User $user): void
{
    $user->save();
    Mail::to($user)->send(new WelcomeMail($user));
}

// GOOD
public function save(User $user): void { $user->save(); }
public function sendWelcomeEmail(User $user): void { Mail::to($user)->send(new WelcomeMail($user)); }
```

## Use descriptive names

```php
// BAD
public function handle($data) { ... }

// GOOD
public function calculateMonthlyRevenue(Collection $transactions): Money { ... }
```

## Prefer fewer arguments

```php
// BAD
public function createUser(string $name, string $email, string $phone, string $address): User { ... }

// GOOD
public function createUser(CreateUserData $data): User { ... }
```

## No side effects

```php
// BAD
public function isValidPassword(string $password): bool
{
    if (strlen($password) < 8) return false;
    Session::regenerate(); // hidden side effect
    return true;
}

// GOOD
public function isValidPassword(string $password): bool
{
    return strlen($password) >= 8;
}
```

## Don't use flag arguments - split into separate methods

```php
// BAD
public function getUsers(bool $isActive): Collection
{
    return $isActive ? User::where('active', true)->get() : User::all();
}

// GOOD
public function getActiveUsers(): Collection { return User::where('active', true)->get(); }
public function getAllUsers(): Collection { return User::all(); }
```

## Avoid negative conditionals

```php
// BAD
if (!$user->isNotVerified()) { ... }

// GOOD
if ($user->isVerified()) { ... }
```

## Avoid logical dependency on implicit class state

```php
// BAD - depends on $this->reportType being set elsewhere
public function generateReport(): string
{
    return $this->reportType === 'pdf' ? $this->toPdf() : $this->toCsv();
}

// GOOD - explicit parameter
public function generateReport(ReportType $type): string
{
    return match ($type) {
        ReportType::Pdf => $this->toPdf(),
        ReportType::Csv => $this->toCsv(),
    };
}
```
